WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:48.010
A Man Who Talks of Dreams and
The King of Undersea Search!"

3
00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:55.300
<b>People's Dreams</b>

4
00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.020
Look at 'em!

5
00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:02.190
How are they still standing?

6
00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:03.980
Ha! Yeah, Bellamy,

7
00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:07.020
wipe the floor with that
green haired freak!

8
00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:08.370
This town ain't
for no dreamin' cowards!

9
00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:11.130
Show that pansy
the meaning of pain!

10
00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:14.800
What's all the commotion about?

11
00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:16.010
I heard Bellamy's pirates

12
00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:17.340
are holding a lynching in there.

13
00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:18.340
Luffy! Zoro!

14
00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:20.430
Why are you letting them
beat you like that?

15
00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:21.900
Go ahead and fight back!

16
00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:24.750
You guys can take them,
no problem!

17
00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:27.110
It's no use lady.

18
00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:28.460
They're too smart for that.

19
00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.050
They've obviously
come to the realization

20
00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:32.800
that they're way out
of our their league.

21
00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:35.340
Refusing to fight
a stronger opponent.

22
00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:37.760
It's disgraceful
but it is smart.

23
00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.650
Clearly the runt lacks
any dignity as a captain.

24
00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:43.610
The Marines
sure are generous these days

25
00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.860
to be willing to
fork over 30 million

26
00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.250
for the head of a worthless,
smart‐mouthed child.

27
00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:53.900
Zoro, no matter what
happens, don't fight back.

28
00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:58.660
Come on, fight back.

29
00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.290
Sounds nice, huh?

30
00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:03.020
The doctrine of non‐resistance.

31
00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.130
So you're weak
and you have no pride.

32
00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.510
You refuse to get into a fight.

33
00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:16.050
And your head is swimming
with silly daydreams.

34
00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:19.060
They sound like children.

35
00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.270
More like little girls!

36
00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.950
My work here is done!

37
00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:32.950
When I heard a bounty worth
30 mill was in town,

38
00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:37.250
I wondered what kind of a
bad ass crook came with it.

39
00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:40.080
Needless to say,
I'm more than a little letdown.

40
00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.810
I'm bored with these cowards!

41
00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:56.840
Quick. Get them out of my face.

42
00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:59.660
Bye ladies.

43
00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:06.790
He tumbled over like a gymnast!

44
00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:17.490
Luffy! Zoro!

45
00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:21.230
Hey, sweet thing,

46
00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:23.060
if you keep hanging out
with these losers.

47
00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.060
you're gonna get left behind.

48
00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.900
Especially when the
new era rolls around.

49
00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.260
What if I bought you?

50
00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.090
You seem like a simple girl.

51
00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:34.470
You can't fetch
too high of a price.

52
00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:36.100
Excuse me?

53
00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:38.560
Did you say you want to buy me?

54
00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.540
That's right.
Come on girl.

55
00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:42.010
Join us.

56
00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:48.030
I hate to say it.

57
00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.590
But I'm too good to be seen
with a pirate like you.

58
00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:53.130
You're nothing
but a small‐time thug.

59
00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:58.140
I like your attitude!

60
00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:04.870
I've never seen
such losers before in my life!

61
00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:17.320
Take your two friends
and get out of my sight.

62
00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:19.820
Before I decide otherwise.

63
00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:21.960
You got that weakling?

64
00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:27.470
Don't ever
show your face in here again!

65
00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:35.350
The sky island does exist.

66
00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:50.360
That place really does
make a killer cherry pie.

67
00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.900
Got something you want to say?

68
00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:54.710
Now what could you
possibly be angry about?

69
00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:58.450
Your two friends won that fight
without even throwing a punch.

70
00:05:58.490 --> 00:05:59.950
Huh?

71
00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:07.750
Ha? You think you'll surpass us?

72
00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:10.730
When next we meet,
we'll both be top pirates.

73
00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:17.220
I respected the way you
treated them back there.

74
00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:19.890
You've got
nerves of steel, lady.

75
00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.310
Huh?

76
00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:24.410
Luffy?

77
00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:32.190
This new era they
keep rambling on and on

78
00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.050
about is a load of crap.

79
00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:38.780
The era when pirates dream of
treasure will come to an end?

80
00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.080
Yeah right!

81
00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.080
What are you talking about?

82
00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:53.870
The dreams of
pirates will never end!

83
00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:58.690
Am I right?

84
00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.250
For someone
shouting as loud as you are,

85
00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:06.510
you sure are talking nonsense!

86
00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:09.360
What are you
talking about dreaming for?

87
00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.610
One upping
your peers isn't easy!

88
00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:15.540
What's with you?

89
00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:17.500
Did you melt your brain?

90
00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:21.880
I wonder what all
the commotion is about.

91
00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:23.490
Forget it.

92
00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:26.120
Those losers are probably
taking out their frustrations.

93
00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:32.810
They can laugh
at us all they want.

94
00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:34.020
Because when you aim high,

95
00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:37.820
you often come across fights
that just aren't worth fighting.

96
00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:38.950
Right?

97
00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:44.250
Let's go.

98
00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.420
Yeah. Uh, Luffy?

99
00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:56.790
Luffy?

100
00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:01.150
Oh, it looks
like I interrupted you.

101
00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.750
Are you in a hurry, kid?

102
00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:05.830
One more thing,

103
00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.880
I hope you find
your way to sky island.

104
00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:27.820
Maybe we should
keep talking to him.

105
00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:30.490
He may know something
about sky island.

106
00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:31.660
Who was he?

107
00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:33.280
I don't know.

108
00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:34.540
And it's not he.

109
00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:36.960
Huh? If it's not he.

110
00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:38.830
Then, what is it?

111
00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:40.130
Probably they.

112
00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:41.500
Come on, let's go.

113
00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.430
Huh? Uh.

114
00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:44.340
What do you mean they?

115
00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:46.240
Are you saying there
were others with him?

116
00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:48.660
Where? I didn't see anyone.

117
00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:51.240
Hello, are you even listening?

118
00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:58.640
It's a beautiful day
for a bottle of rum!

119
00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:03.050
Board.

120
00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:04.010
Board!

121
00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:07.760
Board.

122
00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:08.550
Board!

123
00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:16.200
Board.

124
00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:17.740
Board!

125
00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:22.850
Seriously.
I know say this all the time,

126
00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:25.400
but one thing I am not
is a ship repairman.

127
00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:26.190
But you're really good

128
00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:27.360
at doing this sort
of thing, Usopp.

129
00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:31.150
I know! It's quite amazing.
I'm incredibly versatile.

130
00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:33.320
I say we trash this
and buy a new ship instead.

131
00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:34.450
Are you out of your mind?

132
00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:37.370
Do you have any idea how
we got our hands on this ship?

133
00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:40.100
Yeah, yeah. I've heard
it a thousand times.

134
00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:43.170
It was given to you by the most
gorgeous girl in your village, right?

135
00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:44.300
Who cares?

136
00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:46.330
It's just plain dangerous
to keep relying on a ship

137
00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:47.130
in this condition.

138
00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:49.210
That's why
I'm repairing it, idiot!

139
00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:51.590
Now get down here
and give us a hand!

140
00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:52.580
Repairs, huh?

141
00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:53.760
This?

142
00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:55.790
It won't hold.

143
00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:56.960
Bite me!

144
00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:59.000
Ha! That face is
hilarious, Usopp!

145
00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:00.720
Oh, you mean this one?

146
00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:04.080
Bite me!

147
00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:05.620
What a couple of idiots.

148
00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:07.210
You guys have any
ideas about dinner?

149
00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.280
Bite me!

150
00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:10.910
Fine, no food for you.

151
00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.160
No, we wanna eat!

152
00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:14.710
I better check to see
how that seagull soup is doing.

153
00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:17.630
I wonder if I could use
the feathers as a garnish.

154
00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:18.500
That could be interesting.

155
00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:23.840
– Salvage! Salvage the sea!
– Salvage! Salvage the sea!

156
00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:27.300
– Salvage!
– Salvage!

157
00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:29.440
Huh. There's something
strange with that ship.

158
00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:33.610
– I know that song!
– I know that song!

159
00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:52.270
L‐Luffy! Zoro!

160
00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:54.360
What happened?
Why are you bleeding?

161
00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:55.820
Nami! Oh no!

162
00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:57.230
Are you all right?

163
00:10:57.280 --> 00:10:58.780
Doctor!

164
00:10:58.820 --> 00:10:59.900
You're the doctor!

165
00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:01.150
Go check them out already!

166
00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:02.860
Ow! Right.

167
00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:06.910
So what happened to you guys?

168
00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:10.790
It looks like you were mauled
by a pack of rabid wolves.

169
00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:12.000
It was pirates.

170
00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:12.920
But we're okay.

171
00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:14.170
Just some scratches.

172
00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:15.180
Yup.

173
00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:17.140
You guys seem to be
okay with everything,

174
00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:19.100
but I certainly am not.

175
00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:20.270
What's wrong with you two?

176
00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:21.340
You are men, right?

177
00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:22.540
When someone provokes you,

178
00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:24.380
the only logical response
would be to pummel their faces

179
00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:26.300
and wipe up the blood
with their friends' faces!

180
00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:27.380
Or better yet,

181
00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:29.670
you should have blown up
the entire, annoying town!

182
00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:32.000
What happened to
all the pacifist talk?

183
00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.460
Ugh! Shut up, Zoro!
What's past is past!

184
00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.040
We're not talking about
ancient history here!

185
00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:38.920
Hey, why is she
in such a bad mood?

186
00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:40.630
She didn't get a
single scratch on her.

187
00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:43.090
Huh. Beats me.

188
00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:44.120
Oh, yeah!

189
00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:46.430
Did you get any information
about sky island?

190
00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:49.050
Sky island...?

191
00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:51.920
Does it even matter anymore?

192
00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:54.090
All I did was say
the words "sky island."

193
00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:55.780
And they all laughed at me.

194
00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:59.130
What the heck was so
funny about me saying that?

195
00:11:59.170 --> 00:12:00.370
Bunch of jerks.

196
00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:01.990
I am the ketchup star.

197
00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:04.350
Guard Point!

198
00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:06.560
It sounds like I missed out
on some excitement here.

199
00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:07.850
How's everyone doing?

200
00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:09.960
Robin! Welcome back my love!

201
00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:12.130
I can draw a bath and
prepare a fruit plate for you

202
00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:13.130
if you're interested!

203
00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:14.150
Hey there, Robin.

204
00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:16.320
Where have you
been all day, huh?

205
00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:18.860
Well, I went shopping
for clothes

206
00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:20.590
and found some
information on Skypiea.

207
00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:22.240
That's right. You're
the one who brought it up!

208
00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:25.080
I was made to look like an
idiot thanks to your big mouth!

209
00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:27.020
Trust me, if this place
turns out to not exist,

210
00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:29.860
I'll throw you overboard
with rocks in your pockets!

211
00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:32.470
Robin, I'd kind of keep
my distance if I were you.

212
00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:34.350
At least for the next two hours.

213
00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:37.190
Just don't rock the boat,
know what I'm saying?

214
00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:39.470
Here you go, Captain.

215
00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:41.620
Ooh, thanks, Robin!

216
00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:43.530
Looks like a normal map.

217
00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:44.530
So what's the big deal?

218
00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:46.280
It's this island.

219
00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:49.370
On the left side is Mock Town,
which is where we are now.

220
00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:50.910
And if you look
on the other side,

221
00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:52.620
you'll see an X on the coast.

222
00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:55.290
Supposedly a man lives
there that was banished

223
00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.090
from this town because
he didn't blend in.

224
00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.130
"Didn't blend in"?

225
00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:02.590
His name is Mont Blanc Cricket.

226
00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:06.010
Apparently, Mr. Cricket talked
about his dreams too much.

227
00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:08.350
Sounds like you have
something in common.

228
00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:14.820
<b>Mouth Bay, Jaya</b>

229
00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:14.820
Captain! All undersea
preparations are operational!

230
00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:16.030
Microphone ready!

231
00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:19.240
Excellent.
Initiate the search sonar!

232
00:13:53.110 --> 00:13:55.190
This is
Utan Diver Number 27!

233
00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:56.780
Sonar response confirmed.

234
00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:59.220
We've detected a
school of fish at nine o'clock!

235
00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:02.270
Judging from their speed,
we're looking at saury fish!

236
00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:05.570
Yeah! Time for a fish fry!

237
00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:06.860
Diver four here!

238
00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:08.200
Sonar response confirmed!

239
00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:12.330
A small sailing vessel has
been detected on the surface!

240
00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:14.240
Excuse me? A vessel?

241
00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:17.060
Determine the exact
direction it's traveling!

242
00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:18.560
It's dead ahead, sir!

243
00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:20.260
Twelve o'clock!

244
00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:23.840
It's already close
enough for visual contact?

245
00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:26.800
Cancel the search and
return to the ship at once!

246
00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:39.230
Well, it didn't take us long
to run into something weird.

247
00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:42.320
Do you think it's that same
salvage boat from before?

248
00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:43.160
Or...

249
00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:45.000
Nah, it might look
like a similar ship,

250
00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:46.830
but it's not Masira's group.

251
00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:49.830
Yeah, cause Chopper and
I saw those guys. Right?

252
00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:51.380
Right. We saw them docking.

253
00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:53.300
Turns out they port
at Mock Town the same

254
00:14:53.340 --> 00:14:54.930
as most ships in these waters.

255
00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.040
They're greedy slime
just like all the others.

256
00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.170
You know those
guys better hope

257
00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:00.420
we don't run into them again.

258
00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:02.920
Hey‐ey‐ey, you guys!

259
00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:05.900
Shut your traps
and pay attention!

260
00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:13.100
<b>Shojo, The Oceanogropher
Big Boss, Shojo Pirates
36-Millon-Belly Bounty</b>

261
00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:09.190
Ha!

262
00:15:09.230 --> 00:15:11.600
Can you believe I actually
got all worked up wondering

263
00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:13.100
who you people were?

264
00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:16.780
Your face looks weird.

265
00:15:16.780 --> 00:15:18.480
What species are you?

266
00:15:18.490 --> 00:15:19.940
I'm human, moron!

267
00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:22.450
Are you telling us you
don't know who Shojo is?

268
00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:24.330
He's only the captain
of the Shojo Pirates

269
00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:26.620
and the world's leader
in undersea search!

270
00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:29.410
I wouldn't make our boss
angry if I were you!

271
00:15:29.460 --> 00:15:31.330
Hey! Now, now.

272
00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:32.420
Hold on.

273
00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:35.790
Huh... It looks like we're
in the same profession.

274
00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:38.840
Were you aware that Crocodile,
who is one of the Seven Warlords

275
00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:41.510
of the Sea,
was defeated recently?

276
00:15:41.510 --> 00:15:43.760
When you consider
my dominating abilities,

277
00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:45.970
that open spot is
as good as mine.

278
00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:47.980
I've been doing
my best to stay patient,

279
00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:51.690
but lately the anticipation
has gotten the best of me.

280
00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:52.740
So your goal is to become

281
00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:54.860
one of the Seven
Warlords of the Sea?

282
00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:56.060
Didn't I just say that?

283
00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:58.670
In any case, since you're
obviously not a threat to me,

284
00:15:58.670 --> 00:16:00.490
so let's get to know
each other personally.

285
00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:01.660
I'll start.

286
00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:03.990
Did you know I haven't had
my hair cut in my entire life?

287
00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:05.770
That's over 25 years!

288
00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:06.650
You're impressed?

289
00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:08.650
And jealous. Admit it!

290
00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:09.860
That's lame.

291
00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:11.650
How dare you!

292
00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:12.780
Watch your mouth, kid!

293
00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:14.740
Settle down, my faithful divers.

294
00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:17.070
I'm not going to let
these foul‐mouthed punks

295
00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:19.030
get away with insulting me.

296
00:16:19.030 --> 00:16:20.240
Take this to heart.

297
00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:23.660
Sail through the tunnel that is
my rage and you will be met

298
00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:27.530
by a sea of blood from
which you'll never escape!

299
00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:28.700
Yeah, whatever.

300
00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:31.700
Move aside, we have places
to go and people to meet.

301
00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:33.770
You just don't get it, do you?

302
00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:35.690
This is my turf,
and if you want to pass,

303
00:16:35.730 --> 00:16:37.740
you'll either pay
the toll or be sunk!

304
00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:38.630
Got it?

305
00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:40.630
What's this guy
mean by his turf?

306
00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:42.910
He's starting to sound
like our old friend Masira.

307
00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:45.170
Huh? Masira said
stuff like that?

308
00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:46.630
What? Masira?

309
00:16:46.670 --> 00:16:49.090
What about Masira?

310
00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:52.660
If you must know we kicked his butt
off our boat, but we didn't think...

311
00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:54.990
You what? Kicked him?

312
00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:56.160
– Easy, boss!
– Easy, boss!

313
00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:58.660
No! How dare you lay

314
00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:00.160
– a hand on my brother!
– Wait, hold on.

315
00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:01.330
Listen to me.

316
00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:04.910
Sure we threw him off our boat,
but I bet he's alive.

317
00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:10.500
Havoc Sonar!

318
00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:27.880
The ship!

319
00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:35.870
So... what are they doing?

320
00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:38.250
Who knows? But it's amazing.

321
00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:41.100
He's destroying his
own ship with his voice.

322
00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:42.230
Back to work everyone!

323
00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:43.730
Let's use this to our advantage

324
00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:45.770
and put some distance
between them and us!

325
00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:47.610
Great idea!

326
00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:49.530
Look! Nami's
not a demon anymore!

327
00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:50.590
Really?

328
00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:51.550
Well, I would hope
she'd be calmer

329
00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:54.680
after letting off all
that steam earlier.

330
00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:56.050
Huh?

331
00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:59.660
Luffy! We've got trouble!

332
00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:00.660
This isn't good!

333
00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:03.000
The waves are moving
faster than I thought!

334
00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:04.190
Oh great!

335
00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:05.740
The ship's starting
to break apart

336
00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:07.780
right where I made all
those repairs today!

337
00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:08.520
Argh!

338
00:18:08.530 --> 00:18:10.280
She's beat up enough already!

339
00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:13.240
If we stay here any longer,
we'll start taking on water!

340
00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:14.740
Full speed ahead!

341
00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.450
We need to get out
of his voice's range!

342
00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:46.650
<b>Mock Town, Western Jaya</b>

343
00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:50.270
I'm telling you,
it was the strangest thing.

344
00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:53.020
This gorgeous woman walks in,
I mean she was a knockout.

345
00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:54.980
She comes up to me,
and leans over the table

346
00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:57.900
and says, "Tell me where
this man named Cricket lives."

347
00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:00.740
Sounds like a bold woman.

348
00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:03.450
Bold? No, she was
more like a maniac!

349
00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:05.280
All of a sudden, these
hands started popping out

350
00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:07.400
from her body and knocking
out everyone in the joint.

351
00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:10.250
I'm telling ya,
it really messed with my head.

352
00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:15.620
I'm confused.

353
00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:18.330
What does tearing up the bar
have to do with Old Man Cricket?

354
00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:19.370
The sea around here

355
00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:21.790
is the unofficial turf of
those monkey brothers.

356
00:19:21.830 --> 00:19:24.000
But if someone actually
wants to have something

357
00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:26.460
to do with that geezer,
then they must have caught

358
00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:27.660
some of his own stupidity.

359
00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:31.250
And no one wants that.

360
00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:34.410
I bet you what that lady's
really after is his gold.

361
00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:35.620
His gold?

362
00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:37.660
I heard
they found some recently.

363
00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:39.120
Yeah? Where at?

364
00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:40.070
Well...

365
00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:41.990
Hey, guys!

366
00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:43.650
Bellamy!

367
00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:46.830
What did
you just say about gold?

368
00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:49.880
This old man that
goes by Cricket.

369
00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:52.920
I'd like to set up
a meeting with him.

370
00:19:58.010 --> 00:20:00.050
What do you know of him?
